/* =========================================================================
   Bordeaux Dashboard — the estates’ own technical sheets
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------
   PROVENANCE: VERIFIED, and CHÂTEAU-SPECIFIC. Every field here is read
   from a fiche technique the estate publishes on its own website, for
   that estate and that vintage alone. It is not an appellation average
   and not a critic’s reading.

   Read this against the two things beside it in the UI, which describe
   the year rather than the wine:
     vintages.js   the season and its character across Bordeaux
     phenology.js  flowering and véraison on the ISVV’s reference plots

   Keyed ‘<estate id>|<vintage>’.
     blend   the declared encépagement of that year’s wine, [grape, %],
             kept only where the percentages add to 100
     harvest the first picking date the sheet names
     yld     hl/ha  ·  alc  % vol  ·  ph  ·  temp  serving °C
     decant  the estate’s own sentence on carafing
     window  the estate’s own sentence on when to drink it
     note    the estate’s own account of the growing season
     src     the file it was read from

   The sheets themselves are the estates’ documents and are not
   redistributed here; only the facts read out of them are.
   ========================================================================= */

